# __APP_NAME__

__PURPOSE__

This is the editable Azure App Platform starter template. It includes:

- a local web surface (`src/web`);
- a real local agent (`src/agent`) with its prompt in `src/agent/prompts/system.md`;
- an Azure AI Gateway configuration boundary (`infra-ai-gateway`);
- a deterministic Streamable HTTP MCP Hosted Skill at `src/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/` exposing `analyze_text` at `/runtime/webhooks/mcp`;
- whole-app `dev-start` and `dev-stop` scripts plus shared `scripts/lifecycle/mcp-skill-{start,stop}` runners.

## Run

Azure App Platform automatically selects available ports before opening a newly
created app. Assignments are saved in `.azure-app-platform/ports.env` (`WEB_PORT`, `AGENT_PORT`, `SKILL_<UPPER_SNAKE_NAME>_PORT` / `SKILL_PORT`).

Start the full local stack (MCP Hosted Skill + agent + web):

### macOS/Linux

```bash
./scripts/dev-start.sh
```

### PowerShell 7

```powershell
.\scripts\dev-start.ps1
```

Stop this app with:

### macOS/Linux

```bash
./scripts/dev-stop.sh
```

### PowerShell 7

```powershell
.\scripts\dev-stop.ps1
```

`POST /api/tools/analyze_text` on the agent invokes the deterministic MCP tool directly with zero LLM calls. `POST /responses` executes `analyze_text` over MCP and synthesizes a grounded reply through Azure AI Gateway, returning HTTP `503` (`gateway_not_configured` or `mcp_skill_unavailable`) when either dependency is unavailable.

